\label{conj1}  
For any $x$, $\mathbb{P}(U_n \leq x) \geq \mathbb{P}(U_n^* \leq x)$. Also, the equality holds for all $x$ if and only if 
$v_1, v_2, \ldots, v_n$ are the vertices of a regular simplex inscribed in the unit sphere in $\mathbb{R}^{n-1}$.

\label{thm:Slepian} 
For any correlation matrix $\Sigma$, the Type I error of the one-sided max-type test in (\ref{one-sided-test}) is no more than $\alpha$. Also, when $\Sigma = \Sigma^*$, 
the Type I error of the test is exactly $\alpha$.
